# lib/ is a COMMITTED build artifact, not source. It is built by `pnpm bundle`
# and committed so `dsh plugin --profile web add <github-url>` works: pnpm
# installs a git dependency as the repository checkout and never runs a build,
# so a package whose entry points are untracked installs into a profile that
# silently has no client half. The npm package carries the same files through
# the package.json `files` whitelist.
#
# Never hand-edit these: change src/ and run `pnpm bundle`. The `ci` workflow
# rebuilds them and fails when the committed copy differs from src/.
#
# `text eol=lf` is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the bundler emits LF, and the CI
# comparison byte-compares a fresh build against the checkout. Without pinning
# the ending here, core.autocrlf would rewrite these on checkout and every run
# would report drift.
lib/** linguist-generated=true -diff text eol=lf
